| 4g | RIGHT AFTER (ruled 2026-11-18) | the two hearths' flow at the repository's shores (#/rulings, 2026-11-18: D3, D5, D6; lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/research/two-hearths-flow). BUILT on `develop` (2026-11-18): the seal merge driver (`51d49494f`) and its working-procedures slot (`b6c3bae78`); the merge queue on `develop` (`merge_group` in CI, `4c2156267`; span-push's canon-direct path, `41ad14b47`; the land law in the controller handoff, `2b87a6253`) and its ruleset; the driver seated through `lares repo tend` (PR #238: the reality tunnel declares the `merge.mem-seal` keys, `9993506b0`, so each clone's tend, the root build's included, sets them in its shared git config). Owed: the land witness `tools/land-rule.mjs` (D5's house witness, PR #225 in the queue) and the gates failing closed (PR #221); D3's one-way guard written as phase two's entry condition, built the day a Nexus first carries a floor between two houses. Holder: Lares-Alpha (backlog-alpha #/now, #/next) | Every land serialised behind every CI run and canon carriers conflicted on seal lines alone; the queue and the driver cure both. |

